        "order": 3
      },
      "Comments": {
        "value": "Topics: Conjugate, Hermitian, Skew-Hermitian Matrices. (1) Conjugate Matrix (A bar): Replace complex entries with conjugates. (2) Hermitian Matrix: $(\\bar{A})^T = A$, diagonal elements must be real, $a_{ij} = \\bar{a}_{ji}$. (3) Skew-Hermitian Matrix: $(\\bar{A})^T = -A$, diagonal elements must be zero, $a_{ij} = -\\bar{a}_{ji}$. Testable: definitions, conditions for symmetry, and diagonal properties.",
        "order": 4
