      "Header": {
        "value": "নির্ণায়কের ধারণা (Concept of Determinant)",
        "order": 2
      },
      "Back Extra": {
        "value": "",
        "order": 3
      },
      "Comments": {
        "value": "Topic: Determinant history and definition. History: Originated for solving linear equations, first appeared in 'The Nine Chapters on the Mathematical Art' (3rd century BC), developed by Cardano and Leibniz. Definition: Determinant is a function of a square matrix, denoted as $|A|$ or $\\text{Det}(A)$. Formula 2x2: $|\\begin{smallmatrix} a & b \\\\ c & d \\end{smallmatrix}| = ad - bc$. Occluded elements: Notation $|A|$ or $\\text{Det}(A)$, 2x2 determinant formula $ad-bc$, and matrix elements $a_1, b_2$ in the 3x3 example.",
        "order": 4
      }
    },
