      },
      "Back Extra": {
        "value": "",
        "order": 3
      },
      "Comments": {
        "value": "Core concept: Adjoint matrix definition. (1) Cofactor matrix: Matrix formed by cofactors $A_{ij}$ of square matrix $A$. (2) Adjoint: Transpose of cofactor matrix, denoted as $\\text{Adj}(A)$. (3) Process: Find cofactors, form matrix, then transpose rows to columns. Testable: Definition of cofactor matrix, notation $\\text{Adj}(A)$, and the transpose operation.",
        "order": 4
      }
    },
