      "Comments": {
        "value": "Topic: Determinant identity proof. Goal: Prove $\\begin{vmatrix} 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & p & p^2 \\\\ 1 & p^2 & p^4 \\end{vmatrix} = p(p-1)^2(p^2-1)$. Method: Row operations $R_1' = R_1 - R_2$ and $R_2' = R_2 - R_3$. Factor out $(1-p)$ from rows. Simplify to reach R.S. Key steps: factoring common terms, expanding $2 \\times 2$ determinant, and sign adjustment $(1-p)^2 = (p-1)^2$.",
