        "value": "Core concept: Determinant expansion and cofactor properties. Given determinant $\\Delta = |a_i, b_i, c_i|$, prove $a_2A_1 + b_2B_1 + c_2C_1 = 0$. $A_1, B_1, C_1$ are cofactors of $a_1, b_1, c_1$. Property: Sum of products of elements of one row/column with cofactors of another row/column is zero. Occluded elements: The final expansion steps and the proof conclusion.",
