      "Comments": {
        "value": "Topic: Proving determinant equals zero without expansion. Method: Multiply rows/columns by constants to create identical columns. Key steps: (1) Multiply $C_1$ by $a, b, c$ respectively, (2) Factor out $abc$, (3) Apply operation $C_1 = C_1 + C_3$ to get column of $(a+b+c)$, (4) Factor out $(a+b+c)$ leaving two identical columns of $1$s. Result: Determinant is $0$ because two columns are identical.",
